<h3 data-start=3D"5590" data-end=3D"5619" class=3D"">D=C3=A9tails suppl=C3=
=A9mentaires :</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"5621" data-end=3D"6211">
<li data-start=3D"5621" data-end=3D"5903" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5624" data-end=3D"5650" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
624" data-end=3D"5647"><code data-start=3D"5626" data-end=3D"5636">Provider=
</code> de Redux</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5654" data-end=3D"5903">
<li data-start=3D"5654" data-end=3D"5899" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5656" data-end=3D"5899" class=3D"">Le <code data-start=3D"=
5659" data-end=3D"5669">Provider</code> de Redux enveloppe l'application en=
ti=C3=A8re, ce qui permet d'avoir acc=C3=A8s au store Redux partout dans l'=
application. Le store contient l'=C3=A9tat global de l'application (par exe=
mple, l'utilisateur connect=C3=A9, les donn=C3=A9es du panier, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5904" data-end=3D"6211" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5907" data-end=3D"5924" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
907" data-end=3D"5922">Redux Store</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5928" data-end=3D"6211">
<li data-start=3D"5928" data-end=3D"6211" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5930" data-end=3D"6211" class=3D"">Le store est initialis=
=C3=A9 dans un fichier =C3=A0 part, par exemple, <code data-start=3D"5991" =
data-end=3D"6001">store.js</code>, et contient des r=C3=A9ducteurs qui d=C3=
=A9finissent l'=C3=A9tat global de l'application. Les composants qui doiven=
t acc=C3=A9der =C3=A0 cet =C3=A9tat peuvent utiliser les hooks <code data-s=
tart=3D"6151" data-end=3D"6164">useSelector</code> et <code data-start=3D"6=
168" data-end=3D"6181">useDispatch</code> pour lire ou modifier l'=C3=A9tat=
.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
